<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Claude Debussy</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1862">1862</a>–<a href="/years/1918">1918</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Achille Claude Debussy</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Claude Debussy was a French composer, born in Saint-Germain-en-Laye, who is sometimes seen as the first Impressionist composer, a term he rejected. Admitted to the Conservatoire de <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> at ten, he reached international fame in 1902 with Pelléas et Mélisande, the only opera he completed. His orchestral works include Prélude à l'après-midi d'un faune (1894), Nocturnes and La mer (1903–1905), and his piano works 24 Préludes and 12 Études. Influenced by the Symbolist poets and by Russian and Far Eastern music, he reacted against Wagner and the German tradition. He died of cancer at his home in Paris in 1918, aged 55.</p></div>
